the support of the North.

753
01:04:05.762 --> 01:04:07.406
<i>Well. it was all
about history.</i>

754
01:04:07.430 --> 01:04:09.641
<i>There were pledges that
were made back in the day.</i>

755
01:04:09.766 --> 01:04:14.312
and Jace is sent to remind
Cregan Stark of those pledges.

756
01:04:14.646 --> 01:04:17.148
If your greybeards can fight.
the Queen will have them.

757
01:04:17.315 --> 01:04:20.610
They will fight hard.
like Northerners.

758
01:04:23.238 --> 01:04:25.740
<i>Rhaenyra heard the
news that Luke has died</i>

759
01:04:25.907 --> 01:04:27.157
on a mission that
she sent him on.

760
01:04:27.158 --> 01:04:28.451
so there's guilt involved.

761
01:04:28.576 --> 01:04:31.663
<i>And she's a mother
who's lost a son</i>

762
01:04:31.788 --> 01:04:32.580
and has to go through

763
01:04:32.581 --> 01:04:34.623
the sort of necessary
grieving process

764
01:04:34.624 --> 01:04:36.458
that Daemon. her husband.

765
01:04:36.459 --> 01:04:38.920
<i>can't really appreciate
or understand.</i>

766
01:04:39.170 --> 01:04:41.964
She goes and tries to make
peace with Luke's demise.

767
01:04:41.965 --> 01:04:43.045
but she cannot settle in it

768
01:04:43.133 --> 01:04:44.413
because it is
unsettled business.

769
01:04:44.467 --> 01:04:46.845
until part of Arrax
washes ashore.

770
01:04:47.012 --> 01:04:50.472
Going in search of evidence is

771
01:04:50.473 --> 01:04:52.266
<i>quite fundamentally
important to her.</i>

772
01:04:52.267 --> 01:04:56.645
<i>I guess one of the sort of
maddest things about death</i>

773
01:04:56.646 --> 01:04:58.148
<i>is that it seems
sort of impossible.</i>

774
01:04:58.481 --> 01:05:01.775
especially because really the
overriding feeling often is

775
01:05:01.776 --> 01:05:03.152
<i>you just sit with the absence.</i>

776
01:05:03.153 --> 01:05:06.031
<i>And so. anything that has.
like. a tangibility about it</i>

777
01:05:06.156 --> 01:05:07.698
I think is vitally important.

778
01:05:07.699 --> 01:05:11.036
<i>Her son's cloak. the
wing of his dragon.</i>

779
01:05:11.161 --> 01:05:12.661
I think it's devastating.

780
01:05:12.662 --> 01:05:17.042
<i>but I think it galvanizes
a vengeful feeling.</i>

781
01:05:17.375 --> 01:05:20.170
one that maybe she hasn't paid
so much mind to previously.

782
01:05:24.674 --> 01:05:27.153
<i>I think that Rhaenys is
probably one of the few people</i>

783
01:05:27.177 --> 01:05:28.886
<i>that Daemon knows
he can't mess with.</i>

784
01:05:28.887 --> 01:05:30.847
although I suspect
probably wants to.

785
01:05:32.349 --> 01:05:33.891
We're going to King's Landing.

786
01:05:33.892 --> 01:05:35.977
- To what end?
- Killing Vhagar.

787
01:05:36.353 --> 01:05:38.187
When those two meet.
it's kind of like

788
01:05:38.188 --> 01:05:42.901
a panther meets a
kind of electric eel.

789
01:05:43.026 --> 01:05:45.236
<i>Really dangerous combination.</i>

790
01:05:45.653 --> 01:05:49.032
He's essentially ready to
go to war and get payback.

791
01:05:49.491 --> 01:05:51.158
<i>It was nice to throw
those characters</i>

792
01:05:51.159 --> 01:05:52.827
<i>into conflict with one another.</i>

793
01:05:53.244 --> 01:05:55.829
I think you can tell
from even her demeanor

794
01:05:55.830 --> 01:05:57.582
the way Rhaenys
thinks of Daemon.

795
01:05:57.707 --> 01:05:59.583
Daemon believes that
he's. of course.

796
01:05:59.584 --> 01:06:00.584
completely in the right

797
01:06:00.710 --> 01:06:02.879
<i>and has the power to
order Rhaenys around.</i>

798
01:06:03.046 --> 01:06:04.214
Fly with me.

799
01:06:05.590 --> 01:06:06.675
It is a command.

800
01:06:06.925 --> 01:06:08.677
Would that you were the king.

801
01:06:09.427 --> 01:06:10.863
Where is Jaehaerys?

802
01:06:10.887 --> 01:06:12.263
What do you need of him?

803
01:06:12.555 --> 01:06:14.099
I'm taking him to
the Small Council.

804
01:06:14.724 --> 01:06:17.018
He'll be king one day. He
must begin his instruction.

805
01:06:17.227 --> 01:06:19.270
What if he does not
want to be king?

806
01:06:20.772 --> 01:06:21.772
Where is he?

807
01:06:21.898 --> 01:06:23.399
One of the things I loved
about <i>Game of Thrones</i>

808
01:06:23.400 --> 01:06:24.525
was the character humor.

809
01:06:24.526 --> 01:06:26.277
And. you know. we can
spend a lot of time

810
01:06:26.403 --> 01:06:27.444
<i>being dour in this world.</i>

811
01:06:27.445 --> 01:06:28.904
<i>and it's so important
to have humor.</i>

812
01:06:28.905 --> 01:06:30.030
<i>And when I first saw</i>

813
01:06:30.031 --> 01:06:31.573
what Tom Glynn-Carney
was doing with Aegon.

814
01:06:31.574 --> 01:06:33.867
I thought. "He's finding humor
where I didn't know it existed."

815
01:06:33.868 --> 01:06:35.077
<i>And it's painful.</i>

816
01:06:35.078 --> 01:06:36.704
<i>a guy who's way
in over his head.</i>

817
01:06:36.705 --> 01:06:38.122
who really wants to do well

818
01:06:38.123 --> 01:06:39.957
but just can't make
a right move...

819
01:06:39.958 --> 01:06:42.085
no matter what he does.

820
01:06:42.460 --> 01:06:44.629
Aegon the Magnanimous.

821
01:06:44.796 --> 01:06:46.381
Hail King Aegon!

822
01:06:47.257 --> 01:06:48.633
The Magnanimous?

823
01:06:50.468 --> 01:06:52.761
I think Aegon is
the kind of father

824
01:06:52.762 --> 01:06:55.640
that encourages bad behavior
because he finds it funny.

825
01:06:55.765 --> 01:06:56.766
<i>He loves his kids.</i>

826
01:06:56.891 --> 01:06:58.267
<i>I have no doubt about that.</i>

827
01:06:58.268 --> 01:06:59.601
<i>He loves his kids dearly.</i>

828
01:06:59.602 --> 01:07:02.229
<i>But he's not one
to discipline them.</i>

829
01:07:02.230 --> 01:07:04.149
If anything. he's. you know.

830
01:07:04.274 --> 01:07:05.607
having competitions
with his children

831
01:07:05.608 --> 01:07:07.819
to see who can be
the most rebellious.

832
01:07:08.111 --> 01:07:09.611
<i>And Aegon often wins.</i>

833
01:07:09.612 --> 01:07:10.612
He took my piece.

834
01:07:10.780 --> 01:07:12.824
Is the heir to the throne
bothering you. Tyland?

835
01:07:13.575 --> 01:07:15.493
We see him come into a
Small Council meeting

836
01:07:15.618 --> 01:07:16.494
with Jaehaerys.

837
01:07:16.619 --> 01:07:19.164
and. you know. he's
spurring him on.

838
01:07:19.289 --> 01:07:22.750
He's wanting him to be more
of a... more of a rebel.

839
01:07:22.751 --> 01:07:25.462
more of a nuisance.
just like his old man.

840
01:07:25.587 --> 01:07:28.172
- I think he wants a ride.
- Your Grace.

841
01:07:28.173 --> 01:07:30.008
- A ride?
- A pony ride.

842
01:07:30.759 --> 01:07:32.134
Wouldn't that be fun. Jaehaerys?

843
01:07:32.135 --> 01:07:34.512
Should the Master of
Coin be your royal steed?

844
01:07:35.972 --> 01:07:37.473
It's meant to be a
moment of fun. a bit.

845
01:07:37.474 --> 01:07:40.642
And yes. like Aegon brings
his four-year-old to work.

846
01:07:40.643 --> 01:07:42.811
<i>But I think on a perhaps
nuanced character level.</i>

847
01:07:42.812 --> 01:07:45.439
this is the thing that
Viserys never did for Aegon.

848
01:07:45.440 --> 01:07:47.316
And Aegon did not study
at the feet of his father.

849
01:07:47.317 --> 01:07:49.777
His father had his male heir
and then essentially said.

850
01:07:49.778 --> 01:07:52.030
"Well. that box is
ticked." He was ill.

851
01:07:52.322 --> 01:07:53.655
<i>I think he enjoyed having a son.</i>

852
01:07:53.656 --> 01:07:55.991
<i>but didn't put in the work
the way he did with Rhaenyra</i>

853
01:07:55.992 --> 01:07:57.117
<i>when he was a younger man.</i>

854
01:07:57.118 --> 01:07:58.828
And I think Aegon resents that

855
01:07:59.037 --> 01:08:00.496
and feels that
part of the reason

856
01:08:00.497 --> 01:08:02.164
that he's not seen
as being suited

857
01:08:02.165 --> 01:08:04.334
for the crown or the throne

858
01:08:04.501 --> 01:08:07.379
is because he didn't get that
training from his father.

859
01:08:07.504 --> 01:08:10.048
so now he's going to
make up for that tenfold

860
01:08:10.173 --> 01:08:11.341
<i>with Jaehaerys.</i>

861
01:08:13.885 --> 01:08:16.053
<i>Alicent's been in a
marriage that was loving.</i>

862
01:08:16.054 --> 01:08:20.015
but not exactly romantic or
physical for quite some time.

863
01:08:20.016 --> 01:08:21.850
Cole has got a lot of issues.

864
01:08:21.851 --> 01:08:23.310
<i>One thing I love
about the character</i>

865
01:08:23.311 --> 01:08:25.063
<i>is that he is a knight
in shining armor</i>

866
01:08:25.188 --> 01:08:26.468
and sort of classically handsome

867
01:08:26.523 --> 01:08:28.649
and probably the most messed
up person in the story

868
01:08:28.650 --> 01:08:29.650
in many ways.

869
01:08:29.818 --> 01:08:31.671
<i>You know. clinging to
notions of purity and duty</i>

870
01:08:31.695 --> 01:08:34.322
<i>and just flagrantly breaking
them left and right.</i>

871
01:08:34.698 --> 01:08:36.031
So. there's a lot
of complex things

872
01:08:36.032 --> 01:08:37.866
driving the moves
closer and closer

873
01:08:37.867 --> 01:08:39.077
between Alicent and Cole.

874
01:08:39.369 --> 01:08:40.536
And it takes a leap forward.

875
01:08:40.537 --> 01:08:41.817
<i>But nothing is simple with them.</i>

876
01:08:41.871 --> 01:08:43.748
<i>so for every leap forward.
there's a push back.</i>

877
01:08:44.082 --> 01:08:46.668
We cannot... again.

878
01:08:46.918 --> 01:08:48.669
<i>There's a lot of
wonderful tension there.</i>

879
01:08:48.670 --> 01:08:51.839
I mean. I think there's love.
but there's a lot of mess too.

880
01:08:53.341 --> 01:08:54.842
- Your Grace.
- Good day.

881
01:08:54.843 --> 01:08:56.344
<i>I think. ultimately.</i>

882
01:08:56.553 --> 01:09:01.725
they're two very lost people
in a pretty unforgiving world.

883
01:09:02.058 --> 01:09:04.393
And I think there's always been.

884
01:09:04.394 --> 01:09:06.438
<i>you know. since the
very first episode.</i>

885
01:09:06.563 --> 01:09:08.355
<i>Alicent. you know. had
her eye on Criston Cole.</i>

886
01:09:08.356 --> 01:09:10.357
<i>And then she was a young lady.</i>

887
01:09:10.358 --> 01:09:13.737
<i>and now she's the Queen
of the Seven Kingdoms.</i>

888
01:09:14.237 --> 01:09:16.739
<i>It's paramount that
she keeps it a secret</i>

889
01:09:16.740 --> 01:09:19.950
because not only
would her respect

890
01:09:19.951 --> 01:09:22.077
completely disintegrate.

891
01:09:22.078 --> 01:09:24.538
<i>but her stay in the castle.</i>

892
01:09:24.539 --> 01:09:27.291
And Aegon is so unpredictable.
Who knows what he would do

893
01:09:27.292 --> 01:09:31.128
if he found out that his
mother was having sex

894
01:09:31.129 --> 01:09:33.298
with his Commander
of the Kingsguard?

895
01:09:33.423 --> 01:09:35.215
I mean. not only is
it an embarrassment.

896
01:09:35.216 --> 01:09:38.887
<i>it would bring deep. deep shame.</i>

897
01:09:42.432 --> 01:09:45.101
I want Aemond Targaryen.

898
01:09:46.478 --> 01:09:49.147
Rhaenyra has literally one
line in the first episode.

899
01:09:49.272 --> 01:09:50.440
and the one line she says.

900
01:09:50.774 --> 01:09:52.942
Daemon takes as
pulling the trigger.

901
01:09:53.109 --> 01:09:55.779
In our first episode. we
see him unleash something

902
01:09:55.904 --> 01:09:58.281
that is sort of famous in the
lore of <i>House of the Dragon.</i>

903
01:09:58.448 --> 01:10:00.492
<i>a nasty event that he triggers.</i>

904
01:10:00.950 --> 01:10:04.662
When Rhaenyra declares
that she wants Aemond.

905
01:10:04.788 --> 01:10:09.668
<i>I think it's an admission of
a possibly shameful desire.</i>

906
01:10:09.793 --> 01:10:12.796
<i>and I think that admission
is made directly to Daemon.</i>

907
01:10:12.962 --> 01:10:15.964
I think it's also an
admission of their similarity.

908
01:10:15.965 --> 01:10:18.968
<i>She sort of discloses
another way in which</i>

909
01:10:19.094 --> 01:10:21.805
<i>they actually share a darkness.</i>

910
01:10:22.472 --> 01:10:25.349
"I want Aemond Targaryen"
becomes the battle cry

911
01:10:25.350 --> 01:10:27.643
that then resonates
across the entire season

912
01:10:27.644 --> 01:10:30.312
because that is the
next domino to fall

913
01:10:30.313 --> 01:10:32.940
<i>in this back and forth
that sets in motion</i>

914
01:10:32.941 --> 01:10:34.859
<i>a horrible attack
and counterattack</i>

915
01:10:34.984 --> 01:10:35.984
<i>that continues.</i>

916
01:10:36.111 --> 01:10:38.488
<i>and the atrocities grow
worse and worse as they go.</i>

917
01:10:38.988 --> 01:10:40.656
<i>In our story. it's Mysaria.</i>

918
01:10:40.657 --> 01:10:42.825
who has got her tentacles into
every part of King's Landing.

919
01:10:42.826 --> 01:10:44.993
who is able to provide
the connections

920
01:10:44.994 --> 01:10:47.371
for Daemon to exact revenge.

921
01:10:47.372 --> 01:10:48.997
<i>I think it really is a
big deal for the fans</i>

922
01:10:48.998 --> 01:10:50.438
<i>because it keeps
getting referred to.</i>

923
01:10:50.500 --> 01:10:52.459
And I don't know the
characters' actual names.

924
01:10:52.460 --> 01:10:54.712
They're forever in lore
as Blood and Cheese.

925
01:10:54.713 --> 01:10:57.131
Who the fuck is she?

926
01:10:57.132 --> 01:10:58.674
She's the Queen. she is.

927
01:10:58.675 --> 01:11:00.634
"A son for a son." he said.

928
01:11:00.635 --> 01:11:02.177
The boldest thing that
I think we did there

929
01:11:02.178 --> 01:11:04.889
was decide to give the last
ten minutes of the episode

930
01:11:05.015 --> 01:11:07.517
over to these two characters
that we have never met before

931
01:11:07.642 --> 01:11:10.394
<i>and rely on them to take us
through the end of the story</i>

932
01:11:10.395 --> 01:11:12.021
and to see. hopefully.

933
01:11:12.022 --> 01:11:14.023
as they go deeper and
deeper into the Red Keep

934
01:11:14.024 --> 01:11:16.002
and as we're spending more
and more screen time on them

935
01:11:16.026 --> 01:11:18.403
that something horrible is
going to happen in there.

936
01:11:18.528 --> 01:11:20.863
and knowing that you're
watching <i>Game of Thrones</i>

937
01:11:20.864 --> 01:11:23.700
and you don't know what is going
to come for you from where.

938
01:11:23.908 --> 01:11:25.826
<i>And seeing that play
out hopefully is the fun</i>

939
01:11:25.827 --> 01:11:28.747
and the horror for the
audience that's yet to come.
